ReaComposeM requires the following separate REAPER extensions to be
installed (each via ReaPack) -- the script checks for all three at
startup and refuses to run with an error message if any is missing.
Each is under its own license; none of them is bundled with or
distributed alongside this script, so no license text is included
here, but their use should be mentioned wherever ReaComposeM's own
requirements are documented:
  - ReaImGui (MIT License, Christian Fillion) -- required
  - js_ReaScriptAPI (Julian Sader) -- required
  - SWS/S&M extension (Tim Payne, Jeffos, and contributors) -- required;
    used for reading REAPER's own envelope-range preferences
    (volume/pitch/tempo) in lib/CommonFunction/ScaleConverter.lua

The two files under scales/ (48TET.scl, just_major.scl) contain only
plain interval ratios/cents values for standard, well-known tuning
systems (48 equal divisions of the octave; the classic 5-limit just
intonation major scale) -- mathematical facts, not creative expression,
and not covered by any third-party copyright.
